.TH "INSPEKT\-REPLAY" "1" "2026\-04\-16" "Inspekt 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inspekt\-replay \- Replay recorded browser interactions from a YAML
file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]inspekt\f[R] \f[B]replay\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]]
[\f[I]RECORDING_FILE\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Replay recorded browser interactions from a YAML file.
.PP
Plays back a previously recorded session, reproducing all user actions
with precise timing and visual feedback.
.PP
\f[B]Key Options:\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-speed N\f[R]: Playback speed multiplier (e.g., 2.0 for 2x)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-slow\f[R]: Half speed (0.5x)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-instant\f[R]: Skip delays, execute actions immediately
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-step\f[R]: Pause after each step (press Enter to continue)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-video\f[R]: Generate MP4 video of the replay
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-smooth\f[R]: Smooth video recording (experimental)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-assertions\f[R]: Verify expected state after each step
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-loop N\f[R]: Loop playback N times
.PP
\f[B]Video Options:\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-video\f[R]: Record replay as MP4 video
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-fps N\f[R]: Video frame rate (default: 30)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-crf N\f[R]: Video quality (0\-51, lower is better)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]\-\-smooth\f[R]: Use browser tab capture for smooth video
.PP
If no file is specified, replays the most recent recording.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\f[I]RECORDING_FILE\f[R]
optional path argument
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\(enspeed\f[R], \f[I]FLOAT\f[R]
Playback speed multiplier (e.g., 2.0 for 2x speed, 0.5 for half speed)
(default: \f[CR]1.0\f[R])
.TP
\f[B]\(enslow\f[R]
Half speed (0.5x) \- same as \(enspeed 0.5
.TP
\f[B]\(envery\-slow\f[R]
Quarter speed (0.25x) \- same as \(enspeed 0.25
.TP
\f[B]\(eninstant\f[R]
No delays between steps \- fastest playback
.TP
\f[B]\(enstep\-delay\f[R], \f[I]INTEGER\f[R]
Delay between steps in milliseconds (default: 0, instant)
.TP
\f[B]\(endry\-run\f[R]
Show steps without executing them
.TP
\f[B]\(enstart\-step\f[R], \f[I]INTEGER\f[R]
Start from step number (1\-indexed) (default: \f[CR]1\f[R])
.TP
\f[B]\(enend\-step\f[R], \f[I]INTEGER\f[R]
End at step number (1\-indexed, inclusive)
.TP
\f[B]\(enskip\-hover\f[R]
Skip all hover actions
.TP
\f[B]\(enskip\f[R], \f[I][hover|keypress|type|click|navigate]\f[R]
Skip specific action types (can be used multiple times) (repeatable)
.TP
\f[B]\(enpause\-on\-fail\f[R]
Pause and wait for Enter after each failure
.TP
\f[B]\-v\f[R], \f[B]\(enverbose\f[R]
Show detailed output for each step
.TP
\f[B]\(enno\-visual\f[R]
Disable visual indicators (circle at target, typing indicator)
.TP
\f[B]\(enno\-audio\f[R]
Disable synthesized audio cues for actions
.TP
\f[B]\(enno\-feedback\f[R]
Disable both visual and audio feedback
.TP
\f[B]\(enlock\f[R]
Lock input during replay (hide cursor, ignore keyboard/mouse/scroll)
.TP
\f[B]\-i\f[R], \f[B]\(eninteractive\f[R]
Step through replay manually (Enter=next, Space=skip, Escape=cancel)
.TP
\f[B]\-e\f[R], \f[B]\(enstop\-on\-error\f[R]
Stop replay on first failure (assertion or execution error)
.TP
\f[B]\-T\f[R], \f[B]\(enskip\-tests\f[R]
Skip assertion checks (run actions without evaluating expect conditions)
.TP
\f[B]\(enrestore\-state\f[R]
Restore all captured state (cookies, localStorage, sessionStorage)
.TP
\f[B]\(enrestore\-cookies\f[R]
Restore cookies from recording state
.TP
\f[B]\(enrestore\-storage\f[R]
Restore localStorage/sessionStorage from recording state
.TP
\f[B]\(enverify\-checksum\f[R]
Verify DOM structure checksum matches recording
.TP
\f[B]\(enstrict\-preconditions\f[R]
Halt replay if preconditions are not met (default: warn only)
.TP
\f[B]\(enstrict\-checksum\f[R]
Halt replay if checksum does not match (default: warn only)
.TP
\f[B]\-p\f[R], \f[B]\(enprogress\f[R]
Show compact progress bar instead of step\-by\-step output
.TP
\f[B]\(enskip\-validation\f[R]
Skip preflight validation checks
.TP
\f[B]\(enskip\-ahead\f[R]
Show skip prompt for long delays (default: from config, true)
.TP
\f[B]\(enskip\-threshold\f[R], \f[I]FLOAT\f[R]
Seconds before showing skip prompt (default: from config, 5)
.TP
\f[B]\(envideo\f[R], \f[I]PATH\f[R]
Record replay to video file (MP4/WebM).
Use filename or \(envideo for auto\-naming.
.TP
\f[B]\(ensmooth\f[R]
Record smooth video with continuous frames (larger file, captures
animations)
.TP
\f[B]\(encompact\f[R]
Record compact video with 1 frame per action (smaller file, default)
.TP
\f[B]\(enfps\f[R], \f[I]INTEGER\f[R]
Video frame rate for \(ensmooth mode (5\-30, default: 10).
Ignored in compact mode.
.TP
\f[B]\(enopen\f[R]
Open video file in default application after creation
.TP
\f[B]\(enreveal\f[R]
Reveal video file in file explorer after creation
.TP
\f[B]\(eninclude\-effects\f[R]
Include audio effects in video (click sounds, etc.)
.TP
\f[B]\(enmatch\-viewport\f[R]
Attempt to resize browser to match recorded viewport dimensions
.TP
\f[B]\(enmatch\-zoom\-level\f[R]
Attempt to set browser zoom to match recorded zoom level
.TP
\f[B]\(enfaithful\f[R]
Use captured focus styles for pixel\-perfect keyboard navigation (if
available)
.TP
\f[B]\-n\f[R], \f[B]\(ennative\f[R]
Use native OS keyboard events via AppleScript for keyboard actions
(macOS only)
.TP
\f[B]\(entyping\-speed\f[R], \f[I][instant|fast|normal|slow]\f[R]
Typing speed for native mode: instant, fast, normal (default), slow
(default: \f[CR]normal\f[R])
.TP
\f[B]\(enno\-milliseconds\f[R]
Hide milliseconds in timestamps (default: show milliseconds)
